### 1. Formal Mathematical Objective Function

Define the global state at time \(t\) as the pair
\[
(\eta_{\text{global}}(t),\, \mathcal{L}(t))
\]
where \(\eta_{\text{global}} \in [0,1]\) is system-wide fidelity (1 minus normalized error entropy) and \(\mathcal{L}(t)\) is the measure of agents left behind (population-weighted shortfall across the 17 SDG dimensions).

The ZEM-SDG objective on the horizon \(T = 2125\) is
\[
\max_{\pi} \; \mathbb{E}\left[ \int_{2026}^{T} \eta_{\text{global}}(t) \, dt - \lambda \int_{2026}^{T} \mathcal{L}(t) \, dt \right]
\]
subject to the hard constraints
\[
\begin{align*}
\eta_{\text{global}}(t) &\ge 1 - 10^{-12} && \text{(ZEM floor)} \\
\frac{d\mathcal{L}}{dt} &\le 0 && \text{(no net increase in left-behind measure)} \\
\Delta\eta_{\text{global}} &\ge 0 && \text{under every local policy move (homeostasis)}.
\end{align*}
\]

\(\pi\) is the joint Human–AI–SI governance policy. \(\lambda > 0\) is the ethical weighting that enforces “Leave no one behind” as a first-class term rather than a residual.

Equivalently, in dual form, the problem is to minimize cumulative conflict entropy \(S_{\text{conflict}}\) while maximizing the cooperative surplus generated by shared compute, energy, and knowledge flows.

